  "question": {
    ":question/id": "7bfcce98-dc05-56e9-b37d-ba810da6c2f6",
    ":question/problem": "Find $AB,$ if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-6)\\cdot (-7) & (-6)\\cdot 5 \\\\ 0\\cdot (-7) & 0\\cdot 5 \\\\ 5\\cdot (-7) & 5\\cdot 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}42 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ -35 & 25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
